id: 17
event: tool_call
data: {"session_id":"c8fcac86-a6b3-437d-b5bf-2fadf53a6e6c","seq":17,"kind":"tool_call","payload":{"call":{"command":"cd /workspace && cat > memo.md <<'EOF'\n# MEMO: 2025 Sales Performance Summary\n\n**To:** Leadership Team  \n**From:** Sales Analytics  \n**Date:** 2025-12-31  \n**Re:** Full-year 2025 monthly sales results (fictional data)\n\n## Overview\n\nAcross 12 months and three regions, the company recorded **$5,989,800 in total revenue** on **71,910 units sold**. All regions followed a similar seasonal pattern: steady growth through spring and summer, a September dip, and a strong November–December holiday peak.\n\n## Revenue by Region\n\n| Region | Units | Revenue | Share |\n|--------|-------|---------|-------|\n| North  | 25,710 | $2,125,200 | 35.5% |\n| West   | 24,140 | $1,996,800 | 33.3% |\n| South  | 22,060 | $1,867,800 | 31.2% |\n| **Total** | **71,910** | **$5,989,800** | 100% |\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **North led all regions** for the full year, outperforming South by $257,400.\n- **Best single month:** December 2025, North region — **$218,400** (1,820 units).\n- **December was the strongest month company-wide** ($623,400), roughly 10% of annual revenue.\n- **September was the softest month** ($499,200), consistent with a post-summer slowdown.\n- Regional gaps stayed narrow (top vs. bottom region differed by ~14%), indicating balanced market coverage.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nMaintain the North region's holiday-season playbook as a template, and investigate the September dip for targeted promotions in 2026.\n\n*Attachment: revenue.png (bar chart of revenue by region)*\nEOF\npandoc memo.md -o memo.docx && pandoc memo.md -o memo.pdf && ls -la memo.docx memo.pdf","tool":"bash"},"tool":"bash"},"at":1793936874888}

id: 18
